{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pulls/6738","id":4132377832,"node_id":"PR_kwDOMMa-Ps72TxTo","html_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pull/6738","diff_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pull/6738.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pull/6738.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/issues/6738","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pulls/6738/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pulls/6738/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/issues/6738/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/statuses/6013641abba3c849ea27ecb934627dda217dd57c","number":6738,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Support FastMCP 4 and MCP SDK v2 in `MCPToolset` alongside FastMCP 3","user":{"login":"adtyavrdhn","id":76904033,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2OTA0MDMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76904033?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adtyavrdhn","html_url":"https://github.com/adtyavrdhn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adtyavrdhn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adtyavrdhn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adtyavrdhn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adtyavrdhn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adtyavrdhn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adtyavrdhn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adtyavrdhn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adtyavrdhn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adtyavrdhn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Refs #6661\n\n## Summary\n\n- Support FastMCP 4 and MCP SDK v2 while retaining FastMCP 3 compatibility, behind the existing `MCPToolset` API.\n- Widen the FastMCP dependency range to `>=3.3.0,<5`; stable installs stay on FastMCP 3 because FastMCP 4 is prerelease and needs an explicit opt-in.\n- Normalize the camelCase/snake_case wire-field rename and server metadata across SDK generations via a small `_mcp_compat` module; the generation is detected once, from the `Tool.input_schema` field rename.\n- Keep client-side task routing (SEP-1686) a FastMCP 3 concept: SDK v2 sessions never auto-route into the client task path, since a legacy session has none and a modern session is server-directed (SEP-2663). Explicit `use_task=True` selects the `fastmcp-tasks` extension on modern sessions.\n- Treat `serverInfo` as the optional display-only stamp it is on modern sessions; only capabilities are required to connect.\n- Warn, naming the toolset, when a modern session cannot honor server-initiated sampling, elicitation, or `log_level`; diagnose an uninitialized FastMCP 3 client (`auto_initialize=False`) instead of misreporting a modern session.\n- Add a FastMCP 4 CI job and document the preview limitations and task-semantics difference in `docs/mcp/client.md`.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis adapts the existing `MCPToolset` API to FastMCP 3 and 4 concurrently. It does not add a second public MCP API, force prerelease dependencies on existing users, or admit untested FastMCP 5 behavior.\n\nKnown limitations, both deliberate: handlers configured on a pre-built `fastmcp.Client` cannot be detected for the modern-session warning (FastMCP exposes no public accessor), and FastMCP 4 task execution needs `fastmcp-tasks`, which the `[mcp]` extra does not pull; a clear `ImportError` names the package.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 145 MCP and sampling tests pass against FastMCP 3, and the same 145 against FastMCP 4, `fastmcp-tasks`, and MCP SDK v2, locally and in the dedicated `test FastMCP 4 compatibility` CI job.\n- Compatibility field-name pairs are checked against the real `mcp-types==2.0.0` models, so a mistyped snake_case spelling fails in the FastMCP 3 matrix instead of silently reading `None`.\n- Modern-session behavior (era signal, refused server-initiated requests, `set_logging_level` rejection) was verified against a real `fastmcp==4.0.0b1` client; the CI compatibility job now pins `4.0.0b2`.\n- `uv lock --check` passes machine-independently; the `mcp-types` cutoff is timezone-explicit because uv resolves a bare date in the local timezone.\n- Lint, typecheck, formatting, and lock checks pass locally; the full repository gate runs on the PR.\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [ ] Any **AI generated code** has been reviewed line-by-line by the human PR author, who stands by it.\n- [x] No **breaking changes** in accordance with the [version policy](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/blob/main/docs/version-policy.md).\n- [x] **PR title** is fit for the [release changelog](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/releases).\n\n","labels":[{"id":7110547185,"node_id":"LA_kwDOMMa-Ps8AAAABp9JW8Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/labels/feature","name":"feature","description":"New feature request, or PR implementing a feature (enhancement)","color":"a2eeef","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":8402108317,"node_id":"LA_kwDOMMa-Ps8AAAAB9M3_nQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/labels/MCP","name":"MCP","description":"","color":"0052cc","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":9947550509,"node_id":"LA_kwDOMMa-Ps8AAAACUOuTLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic-ai/labels/size:%20L","name":"size: L","description":"Large PR (501-1500 weighted lines)","color":"fbca04","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-07-25T12:43:11Z","updated_at":"2026-08-12T15:20:05Z","closed_at":"2026-08-12T15:20:02Z","merged_at":"2026-08-12T15:20:0